+# Final result: original unresolved, five turns completed
+
+The exact source asks whether the multipoint Seshadri constant of the singular set of every reduced complex line arrangement equals the reciprocal of the maximum collinear subset, where all projective lines are allowed. This packet does not settle that conjecture.
+
+1. An exact finite fat-point-kernel algorithm applies to any effective point set with r<k²; an explicit genus bound controls all possible violating degrees. Seven conic points plus an eighth off-conic point illustrate that arbitrary point sets are different from arrangement singularities.
+2. The Hesse 12-line arrangement has an arrangement-only fractional-cover optimum 6, while an auxiliary-line cover has globally optimal cost 9/2. Its known Seshadri value 1/5 is recovered with credit.
+3. Every arrangement obtained by adding at most two lines to a supersolvable arrangement satisfies the conjecture. A high-multiplicity sufficient class is also proved.
+4. Explicit cyclic-convolution and uniform deletion-budget conditions retain the credited full Fermat value; exact point counts are given.
+5. For every q≥1, a 9q-line Fermat subarrangement has 13q²+3 singular points and exact constant 1/(4q+1). A nonuniform component cover has optimal cost 4q. This is an infinite partial class, not a general resolution or a novelty claim.
+
+All earlier frozen files remain unchanged. Computational controls are finite; infinite and all-degree conclusions depend on the written proofs. Independent review is required before final disposition. No sixth author search.
