+
+Audit all five turns, not only their finite controls. Highest risks: the explicit degree bound's monotonicity threshold, finite-kernel reducible witnesses and exact infimum argument; Hesse auxiliary-line primal/dual constraints and all-lines optimum; the two-extension theorem's outside-pencil cases and k_actual versus k_components; deletion centers and exact loss counts; and every q≥1 incidence, primal and dual certificate in turn5. The turn5 dual certifies only the component-cover optimum, not arbitrary auxiliary-line optimality.
+
+Run python REPLAY_ALL.py from the packet. SymPy is required by the first checker; the other checkers use standard Python. Each stdout must byte-match its frozen receipt. Historical and final file bindings are checked. Sources are checked if a sources/ directory is present, otherwise their explicit omission is reported. Frozen source PDFs are available locally under /workspace/shared/math-30004322/sources for this review; no public claim that an unpopulated checkout validates PDF hashes.
