+# Source/prior gate: 30004322 / OWR-17296-003
+
+The complete Szemberg contribution, printed3295–3297 of OWR53/2019, and the organizers' discussion printed3272 were read. Printed3297 was visually checked. The exact conjecture is epsilon(P²,O(1);Z)=1/mpl(Z) for the finite nonempty singular set of a reduced arrangement of distinct lines. Here mpl is the maximum number of collinear points over **all** projective lines. We work overC, the field used by the contribution's cited Pokora paper and its surrounding context. Empty singular sets from a single line are not assigned1/0; pencils have one point and constant1.
+
+Official source: https://ems.press/content/serial-article-files/46833 . Pokora's original Question3.1 in https://arxiv.org/pdf/1711.09364v3 uses the maximum over arrangement components, which is potentially stronger. Our assigned statement is the all-lines OWR formulation. The imported literature paragraph about global generation/Kollár concerns the adjacent workshop problem and is irrelevant to this target.
+
+The organizers already report a linear-programming approach and resolution for arrangements through12 lines; the report does not include its full proof. Pokora2019 proves particular standard families; Hanumanthu–Roy–Subramaniam's July2024 author manuscript, Question1.1 and discussion before Theorem2.2, still treats the general line-arrangement question as open while proving additional conditional curve-arrangement results. We do not count rechecking these standard families as new source resolutions.
+Primary manuscript: https://www.cmi.ac.in/~krishna/sc-curve-config.pdf .
+General nef/linear-system computation has a substantial prior literature, including Harbourne–Roé https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0309064 . No invention of that method or historical novelty is asserted.
+
+The complete pinned catalog record was read; its research-results alias entry is null. Exact-ID, OWR-alias and Seshadri all-state PR searches returnednone, as did current branch/commit searches and local all-ref branch/log checks. No prior campaign attempt was recovered. Current primary-topic searches found the cited partial results, not a full general proof; this is a bounded check, not a certification of absence.
+
+An eligible five-turn attempt begins with an explicit bounded-degree exact test when |Z|<mpl(Z)². This does not assume that inequality for every arrangement and does not solve the unrestricted conjecture.
